 "duration": 50.75,
 "language": "pt",
 "text": "What if, tonight, the Moon just... disappeared? First, the nights go dark. Really dark. The Moon is the brightest thing in our night sky, and now it's gone. Then, the oceans. The Moon pulls on the sea and makes the tides. Without it, tides shrink to about a third. Coral reefs that spawn under the full Moon lose their signal. Baby sea turtles that crawl toward the bright sea get lost. Animals that hunt by moonlight, and animals that hide from it, lose a rhythm they've had for millions of years. But the scariest part is slow. The Moon keeps Earth's tilt steady, like a hand on a spinning top. Without it, over millions of years, Earth could start to wobble, and the seasons would go wild. Ice ages. Scorching summers. And no more solar eclipses. Ever. Look up tonight. Would you miss it?",
